examples.response:
A man felt the sharp sting of a thorn and immediately reached out to pull it free;
He remembered the warmth of a shared meal and the weight of a promise kept;
He watched a child laugh at a simple game and felt a profound, inexplicable joy;
He stood before a mirror and saw not just a face, but a story of mistakes and triumphs etched in time;
He realized that to be human is to feel the ache of loss and the fierce, unyielding hope for tomorrow.
